  <h2>Done properly, even from far away</h2>
  <p>
    In our tradition, the sankalp is what ties a ritual to a person — and the yajman has never had
    to stand at the altar. Temples have performed pujas for absent devotees for generations.
    Watching live gives you what you'd have in person: hearing your name spoken, folding your hands
    at the aarti, and receiving the blessing as it happens.
  </p>

  <h2>Puja or havan?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Puja</strong> — offerings of lamp, flowers and prayer. Usually 20–60 minutes; lighter, and lovely for daily or festival worship.</li>
    <li><strong>Havan</strong> — offerings into a sacred fire with Vedic mantras. Usually 60–120 minutes or more; chosen for bigger intentions and life events.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Only joy, only blessings</h2>
  <p>
    Every ritual we perform is benefic — for learning, prosperity, health, love, peace and
    celebration. We don't do fear, we don't do fierce rituals, and we never tell you something bad
    will happen if you don't book. A puja should leave you lighter, not worried.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p><strong>Do I need to be present?</strong><br />No. The ritual is done in your name through the sankalp; watching live is your participation.</p>
  <p><strong>What if I miss the live stream?</strong><br />Your sankalp was still performed, and the replay is available for 7 days.</p>
  <p><strong>What is a gotra, and what if I don't know mine?</strong><br />It's your family lineage. If unknown, priests use "Kashyap" by custom.</p>
  <p><strong>Can I include my family?</strong><br />Yes — add their names when you book.</p>
  <p><strong>Will I get prasad?</strong><br />Choose it at checkout and we'll post it after the ritual.</p>
  <p><strong>Are the priests real?</strong><br />Yes — verified, and you'll see them live at the altar.</p>
  <p><strong>Do you do any "dark" or fierce rituals?</strong><br />No. We perform only positive, benefic pujas and havans.</p>
  <p><strong>Do you offer aarti, darshan, astrology or yoga?</strong><br />Not yet. Right now we perform pujas and havans only.</p>

  <div class="note">
    Rituals are performed with devotion by verified priests. Benefits described are those
